  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan: Action Plan for Peace II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Action Plan for Peace (APP) with the immediate goal to stop the war and facilitate processes toward a just, peaceful and reconciled society. This agenda was built against the understanding that it is not only important to stop the war but also build structures and institutions that would not encourage relapse into violence.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Churches, South Sudan Council of Churches, beneficeries of neutral form work like armed groups or local authorities, communities, target communities of reconciliation processes and trauma healing.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved community security and social cohesion providing conditions conducive to a sustainable national reconciliation and enduring national political settlement in South Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the APP I, church leaders coordinated convergence of the two top leaders in the Revitalized Agreement on the Resolution of Conflict in South Sudan (R-ARCSS) and facilitated high level advocacy with the heads of main church denominations &#x2013; the Catholic and Anglican Churches. To this, among other actions, church leaders contributed to holding the country together. This APP II has been developed against the backdrop of extension of the transition period, great steps in the implementation of the Agreement, improved social and political relations and, to some extent, increased knowledge of citizens&#x2019; role and place in the peace process. On the other hand, the context is also informed by situations of increased localised community based violent conflicts.</narrative>
  </description>
